t  an industry with companies that are too  big to fail well you'll apply socialism  there need to spread the costs out of  fixing the environmental damage done by  industry socialize the clean up  capitalism for the profit socialism for  the cost if you have a virus that you  mishandle  leading to an even worse economic  implosion than we would otherwise have  had well just start buying food and  giving it to people in food lines so the  solution here is we should be dealing  with the fragility of the system in a  proactive way instead of reacting in  what is a completely impotent way that  is the problem and the point of social  democracy is you take capitalism but you  commit money to proactively insulating  the system from shocks and calamities  free market capitalism by its nature  doesn't do proactive it's just not in  there it's too expensive it's not  immediately beneficial true free-market  capitalism would not do the proactive  stuff that's why you need the regulatory  framework of social democracy and again  this is the type of stuff Trump said we  would never have here and he's doing it  and he's right to do it I'd that I want  to be clear it's the right it's one of  the right policies given what's going on  the logistical and crony istic elements  of it will of course be a disaster as  always is the case for Trump but the  point is their principles evaporate when  they have a situation like this to deal  with
 

